Of course!  The whole idea is to put a prior on that has zero density on singular matrices!  Maybe that wasn’t clear in my email.

> This is kind of hard to do numerically with the inverse Wishart because the determinant term and the trace term pull in different directions as the covariance matrix approaches being singular. For LKJ it is simply a matter of constraining the shape parameter to be > 1. Also, the decomposition into standard deviations and a correlation matrix makes it easier to deal with the ordering below.
