I'm sure you'll be contributing in short order!

>
> I am aware that there is already considerable effort to 'translate'/make working Stan code for the books I mentioned, and so wanted to ask - has work begun on writing Stan code for Gelman, Hill and other books? I can see that the majority of BUGS book examples are done already. Also, where would be most helpful for me to begin?

Some background:
The example-models repository has just been a place where we have contributed models, without checking for quality. I'm sure not everything there even compiles under Stan. That said, some of them implementations might be the best way to do it. We just haven't systematically verified anything.

Here are some things I think would be helpful:
* discuss how users would use the example-models repository and how we can make that experience better for them. I think one of the things we can do is to provide text descriptions about the models in a standard format.
* create a standard layout for each model; this should include the data and how to run the model
* consistent formatting, perhaps syntax highlighting in the description?
* apply best practices for model building
* place a little bit of process on the repository so everything that gets in meets the standards that we set

Daniel

